# A field that first appears mid-file has no rows before its first value. The array of /arr has 1 element for 100
# messages, 3 for the next 100 and 5 for the last 100: data[1] is 200 samples and data[3] is 100, none invalid. Rows
# written before a column existed are not nulls of it: a reader tells the two apart, and read_series and
# export_series would report 100 or 200 invalid samples the file does not hold.
# Fixture: a ROS 1 MCAP of one topic (std_msgs/Header header, float64[] data), 300 messages 10 ms apart.
# app: -d scripts/qa/regressions/fixtures/growing_array.mcap
# needs: plugins
until read_series {"paths":["/arr/data[0]"]} "count":300
absent "invalid"
read_series {"paths":["/arr/data[1]"]}
expect "count":200
absent "invalid"
read_series {"paths":["/arr/data[3]"]}
expect "count":100
absent "invalid"
expect "duration_s":0.99
